# Status (2026-10-09): fixed the same day: a deadlock is now reported as a Sake ThreadError (lib/sake.rb, Sake.execute).
# A program that deadlocks (here: Queue.pop with nothing left to push) ends with Ruby's own
# `fatal: No live threads left. Deadlock?` and a 60-line Ruby backtrace through lib/sake/*.rb, instead
# of a Sake error with the Sake line (FILE:LINE: in FUNCTION: ...). Seen with monitor.sake when
# `Monitor.synchronize(m) { Monitor.synchronize(m) { } }` is nested without an identity `me`
# (the inner enter waits for a hand-over that only the same thread could give).
q = Queue.new
Queue.pop(q)
